  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Value addition agriculture</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to identify the feasibility of adapting and implementing internationally recognised market-driven food safety and quality management systems in the horticulture sector of Zimbabwe, by executing a feasibility study.This study zooms into the assessment of bottlenecks and opportunities on the level of&#x2022;	client demands. The clients are foreign purchasers of horticultural produce and fruits;&#x2022;	the private sector in Zimbabwe;&#x2022;	the Dutch private sector;&#x2022;	the government in Zimbabwe;&#x2022;	education in Zimbabwe.This study must lead to action plans and recommendations for the Zimbabwean private sector, government and education institutes, on adapting and implementing sustainable market-driven food safety and quality management systems.</narrative>
  </description>
